Verified filename there: bbb_sunflower_1080p_30fps_normal.mp4.zip

Actual downloaded source (the 24 fps film, not that 30 fps ZIP):
https://uploads.video-commander.com/sample/BigBuckBunny.mp4
Mirror publisher: https://github.com/video-commander/public-test-streams
Source size: 158008374 bytes
Source SHA-256: 1cadc5e09cbb81044e256f9fc67090fcf86d7a596145eb615844fe15341451e6

Modifications: trim 01:00 through 06:00, remove audio, resize to 640x360,
transcode to H.264 at 24 fps, and generate a poster and thirty sampled images
with the production YATM native Preview worker, using its 320x180 tile,
10-second interval and 30-frame defaults. The VTT maps the thirty images
to the complete five-minute excerpt. The Demo File's Note carries the credit,
license URL and modification notice.

Transcode tool: FFmpeg 8.1.1, libx264, darwin-arm64.
Native worker: YATM v1.0.0-alpha.2, darwin-arm64, FFmpeg 8.0.

Reproduction from the repository root (PREVIEW_HELPER names a packaged
worker with its adjacent private libraries; no helper is needed to run the
default Demo):

curl --fail --location \
  https://uploads.video-commander.com/sample/BigBuckBunny.mp4 \
  --output /private/tmp/yatm-demo-bbb-source.mp4
ffmpeg -hide_banner -loglevel warning -nostdin -y \
  -ss 60 -i /private/tmp/yatm-demo-bbb-source.mp4 -t 300 -map 0:v:0 -an \
  -vf scale=640:360 -r 24 -c:v libx264 -preset medium -crf 27 \
  -pix_fmt yuv420p -g 48 -keyint_min 48 -sc_threshold 0 -map_metadata -1 \
  -fflags +bitexact -flags:v +bitexact -movflags +faststart \
  internal/demo/assets/big-buck-bunny.mp4

DEMO_ASSETS="$(pwd)/internal/demo/assets"
PREVIEW_OUTPUT=$(mktemp -d)
python3 - "$DEMO_ASSETS" "$PREVIEW_OUTPUT" <<'PY' | "$PREVIEW_HELPER"
import json, sys
print(json.dumps(dict(
    protocol=1, kind="video", source_path=sys.argv[1]+"/big-buck-bunny.mp4",
    output_dir=sys.argv[2], format="png", quality=75,
    poster_width=512, poster_height=512, timeline_width=320, timeline_height=180,
    timeline_interval_seconds=10, timeline_max_frames=30, max_input_pixels=64000000,
)))
PY
cp "$PREVIEW_OUTPUT/poster.png" "$PREVIEW_OUTPUT/timeline.png" \
  "$PREVIEW_OUTPUT/timeline.vtt" "$DEMO_ASSETS/"

